Ibid.: Directly toward Jerusalem in the south of Judah—i.e. at point <big>ת</big> there north–south are forbidden but east–west are permitted. We do not forbid east–west there for “dragging” (<i>gerirah</i>) as with the side directions forbidden for dragging: this spot adjoins only the sides, and the sides were forbidden only because of dragging, so this spot is not “dragged” relative to the sides (a “dragging of dragging”)—and the difficulty stands (<i>v’kushya le-…</i>).
